eq 8$. ... 2025-07-04\n\n# Counting Graph Orientations with No Directed Triangles\n\n  * Pedro Araújo\n  * Fábio Botler\n  * Guilherme Oliveira Mota\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.37236/12923\n\n### Abstract\n\nAlon and Yuster proved that the number of orientations of any $n$-vertex graph in which every $K_3$ is transitively oriented is at most $2^{\\lfloor n^2/4\\rfloor}$ for $n \\geq 10^4$ and conjectured that the precise lower bound on $n$ should be $n \\geq 8$. We confirm their conjecture and, additionally, characterize the extremal families by showing that the balanced complete bipartite graph with $n$ vertices is the only $n$-vertex graph for which there are exactly $2^{\\lfloor n^2/4\\rfloor}$ such orientations.\n\n  * PDF\n\nPublished\n\n2025-07-04\n\nHow to Cite\n\nAraújo, P., Botler, F., & Oliveira Mota, G. (2025). Counting Graph Orientations with No Directed Triangles. The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, 32(3), #P3.2. https://doi.org/10.37236/12923\n\nIssue\n\nVolume 32, Issue 3 (2025)\n\nArticle Number\n\nP3.2--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAn Indicator Formula for the Hopf Algebra $k^{S_{n-1}}\\#kC_n$ (https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.12714)\nciteturn6academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.2 years ago; Title: An Indicator Formula for the Hopf Algebra $k^{S_{n-1}}\\#kC_n$ ... We also derive a variety of counting formulas including Theorem 6.2.2 which fully describes the indicators of all $2$-dimensional irreps of $J_n$ and Theorem 6.1.2 which fully describes the indicators of all odd-dimensional irreps of $J_n$ and use these formulas to show that nonzero indicators become rare for large $n$.\nTitle: An Indicator Formula for the Hopf Algebra $k^{S_{n-1}}\\#kC_n$\nAuthors: Kayla Orlinsky\nDate: Mon Aug 22 20:39:08 2022\n\nThe semisimple bismash product Hopf algebra $J_n=k^{S_{n-1}}\\#kC_n$ for an algebraically closed field $k$ is constructed using the matched pair actions of $C_n$ and $S_{n-1}$ on each other. In this work, we reinterpret these actions and use an understanding of the involutions of $S_{n-1}$ to derive a new Froebnius-Schur indicator formula for irreps of $J_n$ and show that for $n$ odd, all indicators of $J_n$ are nonnegative. We also derive a variety of counting formulas including Theorem 6.2.2 which fully describes the indicators of all $2$-dimensional irreps of $J_n$ and Theorem 6.1.2 which fully describes the indicators of all odd-dimensional irreps of $J_n$ and use these formulas to show that nonzero indicators become rare for large $n$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCounting graph orientations (https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/download/v32i3p2/pdf/)\nciteturn6search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; with no directed triangles ... Submitted: Apr 1, 2024; Accepted: Jan 18, 2025; Published: Jul 4, 2025 ... Alon and Yuster proved that the number of orientations of any n-vertex graph in ... Furthermore, for the strongly connected triangle, denoted by K↻\nCounting graph orientations\nwith no directed triangles\nPedro Ara´ujoa\nF´abio Botlerb\nGuilherme Oliveira Motab\nSubmitted: Apr 1, 2024; Accepted: Jan 18, 2025; Published: Jul 4, 2025\nc© The authors. Released under the CC BY-ND license (International 4.0).\nAbstract\nAlon and Yuster proved that the number of orientations of any n-vertex graph in\nwhich every K3 is transitively oriented is at most 2⌊n2/4⌋for n 󰃍104 and conjectured\nthat the precise lower bound on n should be n 󰃍8. We conﬁrm their conjecture\nand, additionally, characterize the extremal families by showing that the balanced\ncomplete bipartite graph with n vertices is the only n-vertex graph for which there\nare exactly 2⌊n2/4⌋such orientations.\nMathematics Subject Classiﬁcations: 05C35\n1\nIntroduction\nGiven a graph G and an oriented graph 󰂓H, we say that 󰂓G is an 󰂓H-free orientation of G if\n󰂓G contains no copy of 󰂓H. We denote by D(G, 󰂓H) the fam